/-!
# `Work.MotAS.witCert` — explicit polynomial certificates for `Work.MotAS.witValue`

The proof of `Work.MotAS.witValue` is an explicit polynomial computation.  This file contains
the resulting explicit polynomials (computed by a computer-algebra system, over `ℤ`), so that
the identities checked in `witValue.lean` are *linear* in the size of the certificates and can
be closed by `ring`.

With `c = witPt a b` (a point of `K[X]⁵`) put

* `witA1 a b g = asRuleQA (C a) (C b) (C g) c 1`,
* `witA0 a b g = asRuleQA (C a) (C b) (C g) c 0`,
* `witB0 a b g = asRuleQB (C a) (C b) (C g) c 0`,
* `witB1 a b g = asRuleQB (C a) (C b) (C g) c 1`.

Then `witA1 * witB0 - witA0 * witB1` and `(X^5 - X - C g) * witH + witPhi` agree modulo the ideal
`(5) ⊂ ℤ[a,b,g,X]`, and the cofactor is `witZ`:

  `witA1 * witB0 - witA0 * witB1 - ((X^5 - X - C g) * witH + witPhi) = 5 * witZ`  (over `ℤ`).

Consequently the identity holds in any commutative ring of characteristic `5` (in particular in
`K[X]` for `K` a field with `CharP K 5`).

All the polynomials are written in the normal form generated by the `Polynomial.C`-atoms
`Polynomial.C a`, `Polynomial.C b`, `Polynomial.C g` and `Polynomial.X`, with integer coefficients.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

